                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Been having a lot of fun with this throughout its development. \n\nCombat is fast and fun. It's really satisfying to weave through enemies, methodically taking them out in order of current threats. This does get harder to do on the higher floors though, as the enemies will quickly overwhelm you. You'll need a plan of action for that.\n\nThis is a pretty hard game. But it gets easier as you figure out the best ways to take out everything. Or you can just dash up to them and hit them. That works too. If you're bored of melee, there are various spellbooks which can offer you ranged, AoE or other attacks. They don't have any cooldowns, but they can only be used a limited amount of times before you need to find a new spellbook.\n\nThere's a unique way of \"leveling up\" that I like as well. \nRather than getting a guaranteed upgrade of some sort when you have enough exp, you simply get another slot to hold an orb. Orbs float around the tower, each offering a random power up, such as vampirsm, alchemy, pet affinities, or agility. The orbs are fragile however, and will explode violently if hit by a single attack from you or an enemy. While your foes won't target the orbs intentionally, they may unintentionally blow one up while targetting you.\n\nDon't get too confident when you have a lot of items you feel are powerful, though. Just look at the game's name...",
